  "prompt_text": "Use case: precise-object-edit. Edit ONLY the surface detailing in the FIRST image, the current sheep_fleeced sprite sheet. Preserve ALL ten animals, exact 2 rows x5 columns layout, pose, body proportions, position, camera, colours, lighting and alpha. First reference = edit target; deer/person/scene = continuity references. Make both horns completely smooth, with zero ring marks. Simplify fleece to exactly SEVEN broad connected scalloped lobes and TWO broad shadow patches on each visible torso. Remove all interior tiny curls, squiggles, short fur strokes and speckling. Keep main outer wool silhouette organic; broad calm cream wash inside. Main silhouette contour remains twice interior line width. Mark direction upper-left to lower-right. Same restrained natural-history ink and tone as reference deer; no plastic/cartoon/3D render. Do not redraw the poses or rescale individuals. Keep 35deg left S row and right E row. True alpha transparent background, no ground/shadow/text/grid. Do not add any small decorative marks. The primary goal is quiet LARGE planes with a FEW intentional marks, so count the requested marks rather than filling the body with texture.\n",
